{title: My Everything}
{artist: Glenn Fredly}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Cruising when the sun goes [Dm]down
Cross the [F]sea
Searching [Am]for something in[G]side of me
[C]I would find all the lost pi[Dm]eces
Hardly [F]feel deep in [Am]real
I was [G]blinded now I see
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Pre-Chorus}
[Am]Hey Hey [G]hey you’re the one[F]
[F]Hey Hey hey you’re the one
[Am]Hey Hey [G]hey I can’t [F]live without you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Take me [C]to your [Dm]place
Where our [F]heart be[G]longs to[Am]gether
I will follow [G]you
You’re the reason [F]that I breath

I’ll come [C]running to [Dm]you
Fill me [F]with your [G]love for[Am]ever
Promise you one [G]thing
That I would never [F]let you go
‘Cause [Fm]you are my every[C]thing
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]You’re the one, you’re my inspiration
[Dm]You’re the one, kiss, you’re the one
[F]You’re the light that would keep me safe and warm
[G]You’re the one, kiss, you’re the one

[C]Like the sun goes down,
coming [Dm]from above all
To the deepest [F]ocean and highest mountain
[G]Deep and real deep I can see now
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Pre-Chorus}
[Am]Hey Hey [G]hey you’re the one[F]
